    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Goriely & Tabor (1998) PRL / Gerbode et al. (2012) Science Kirchhoff elastic rod tendril perversion, G-fiber overwinding & Pass 3 thigmotropic contact coiling — Source and data traceability: 94/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "`datasets/tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature/` now vendors 5 SHA-256-pinned files (`EXPECTED_SHA256` L110-L127, verified fail-closed by `verify_dataset_integrity` L141-L153): the Pass 2 reference JSON, specimen JPG, scout manifest and bib, plus the new `thigmotropic_contact_coiling_reference.json` in which every value carries a provenance tag (literature / derived / assumption / prediction), Darwin's (1865) Ch. IV timings and support-size statement are quoted with the caveat that they are approximate readings, and a `residual_remediation` list is recorded. The bib gains Jaffe & Galston (1968), Isnard & Silk (2009) and Euler (1762); the README section 5 documents the Pass 3 model and states that the new DOIs were not re-verified offline. Deductions: the two new DOIs could not be verified offline (-2); Darwin's \"25 s to visible curvature\" and \"5-60 min to full wrap\" are approximate readings without page pinpoints (-2); Euler (1762) has no DOI and the capstan law is cited without a page (-1); the bib is pinned but is itself an authored file, so pinning does not establish provenance (-1)." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-source-traceability-1>,
